helpers
=======

Small stand-alone programs which are built and installed alongside Pyxplot.
They share Pyxplot's string-handling and utility code, but not its
interpreter.

pyxplot_fitshelper.c
    An input filter which converts FITS files into plain text, listing the
    headers of each extension and the contents of its tables. Pyxplot runs it
    automatically to read files ending in .fits. Without the cfitsio library,
    it is a dummy which reports that FITS files are not supported.

pyxplot_timehelper.sh
    An input filter: a shell script which uses sed to replace the names of
    days and months with numbers, so that dates written as text can be read by
    Pyxplot. Pyxplot runs it by default to read files ending in .log, such as
    web server logs.

pyxplot_watch.c
    The pyxplot_watch program, which watches a list of script files (which may
    be given as wildcards) and runs Pyxplot on each of them whenever it is
    modified.
